<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dnyaneshwar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1275–1296</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Jnaneshwar, Jñāneśvar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dnyaneshwar was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marathi">Marathi</a> poet-saint who in 1290 completed the Dnyaneshwari, a verse commentary on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a> and one of the founding works of Marathi literature. A key figure of the Varkari devotional movement, he is said to have entered samadhi at Alandi at the age of twenty-one. His shrine there remains a major pilgrimage centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dnyaneshwar.jpg" alt="Dnyaneshwar" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Swapniladitya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dnyaneshwar2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
